com/users/gpinigin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-01-04T04:25:35Z","updated_at":"2017-01-04T04:25:35Z","body":"> If so, can you take a look and see why isNewerThan is evaluating to true in this case? The only way I can see this happening is if the new playlist not only has media sequence set back to 0, but if it also has an end tag appended when the old one didn't.\r\n\r\nEnd tag is appended to the new playlist also. I think appending end tag is the only reason why `isNewerThan` returns `true`\r\n\r\nJust for clarification – due streaming service malfunction in some rare cases client is being redirected from live HLS stream to static HLS VOD. VOD playlist doesn't contain any segments from the preceding playlist.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/270292296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gpinigin","id":2851178,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTExNzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2851178?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin","html_url":"https://github.com/gpinigin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gpinigin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/